WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:08.100 align:start position:0%
A little water, right?
&gt;&gt; It happens so fast.

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:16.800 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Exactly 1 hour after I woke up, the
house rotated 90 degrees and smashed

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:16.800 align:start position:0%
into the bridge.

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:24.100 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; You can't describe it. It's like
everything got picked up

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:27.700 align:start position:0%
and
set down, but all wrong.

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:34.115 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; The city of Asheville's water supply was
more or less decimated.

00:00:32.095 --> 00:00:34.115 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; [music]

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:41.400 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; A friend of mine who lost everything
looked me in the face and he said, hey,

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:45.200 align:start position:0%
we got [music] this, dude.
Don't quit.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:49.700 align:start position:0%
And I just said, well, I won't. I'm not
going anywhere. I'm not quitting on any

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:49.700 align:start position:0%
of you.

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:57.800 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; One shovel at a time, one wheelbarrow at
a time, that is what it's going to take.

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:05.500 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; We had brought my grill and we were just
going to cook some burgers and some hot

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:09.100 align:start position:0%
dogs. And then within a day, we had
hundreds of people show up and want to

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:11.900 align:start position:0%
help.
&gt;&gt; Same thing. [music]

00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:15.900 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; There's a guy today working on my camper
and he drove 11 hours yesterday just

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:20.200 align:start position:0%
because he heard people needed [music]
RV repairs.

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:23.500 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; We got our town to a place that we could
actually

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:26.800 align:start position:0%
get some hope because [music] when we
first saw it, there was no hope.

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:32.500 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; When the rest of the world kind of
forgets what's going on here,

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:32.500 align:start position:0%
it's [music] still there.

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:38.100 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; I think the final result [music] is
years down the road.

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:41.526 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; It's scary because it's like a lack of
funding and we're not sure

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:45.500 align:start position:0%
when those areas are going to come back,
[music] how or if they are even able to

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:48.300 align:start position:0%
come back at all.
&gt;&gt; We're making it together [music]

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:51.100 align:start position:0%
somehow,
one day at a time.

